1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,526
England, 1300. It's November, and tonight you sleep with the cow.

2
00:00:04,552 --> 00:00:08,797
Not near the cow. With her. One roof, one room.

3
00:00:08,797 --> 00:00:13,511
People at this end, animals at that end, and a drain down the middle.

4
00:00:13,536 --> 00:00:17,094
This is not poverty. This is heating.

5
00:00:17,094 --> 00:00:23,570
A grown cow gives off as much heat as a small modern heater. All night. For free.

6
00:00:23,585 --> 00:00:27,616
The fire sits in the middle of the floor. There is no chimney.

7
00:00:27,616 --> 00:00:31,465
The smoke leaves through the thatch, and through your eyes.

8
00:00:31,469 --> 00:00:36,746
Before you sleep, you bury the embers in ash, so they last until morning.

9
00:00:36,746 --> 00:00:43,100
In towns, a bell told you when. Couvre-feu. Cover the fire. Curfew.

10
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:46,881
Not every animal makes it to Christmas. There isn't enough hay.

11
00:00:46,881 --> 00:00:50,357
The old English name for November was blood month.

12
00:00:50,357 --> 00:00:56,823
So you lie down on straw, beside your family, beside the cow, and listen to her breathe.

13
00:00:56,890 --> 00:01:01,585
Not small. Not sad. Just warm enough to reach the morning.
